# healthcheck.hosts — declarative inventory for scripts/healthcheck.{sh,ps1}
#
# One row per device. Whitespace-separated. '#' starts a comment.
# Keep in sync with docs/Devices.md (single source of truth for the inventory).
#
# Columns:
#   name      Display name.
#   ip        Address to probe.
#   role      Free-text group label (node / nas / network / …). Purely cosmetic.
#   ports     Comma-separated TCP ports to probe, or '-' for none (ICMP only).
#             A host with ports is considered UP if ANY listed port is open,
#             even when ICMP is blocked.
#   severity  'critical' → counts against the exit code when down.
#             'optional' → a down host is reported as a warning only
#             (e.g. desktop-01 may be intentionally asleep via the power
#             orchestrator, #191).
#
# name         address                              role     ports        severity
# Addresses are UniFi local-DNS names (Infrastructure/unifi/network.yaml staticDns), not
# IPs: the 192.168.179.x addresses here went stale when the nodes and NAS moved to VLAN
# 1000 (#37), and every row but the gateway reported DOWN from then on. The gateway stays
# an IP because it IS the DNS server.
gateway        192.168.178.1                        network  -            critical
DS1813-01      nas.homelab.chrison.internal         nas      5001,2049    critical
hpe-01         hpe-01.homelab.chrison.internal      node     8006         critical
nuc-01         nuc-01.homelab.chrison.internal      node     8006         critical
hpe-02         hpe-02.homelab.chrison.internal      node     8006         critical
desktop-01     desktop-01.homelab.chrison.internal  node     8006         optional
